# Web app configuration
# Copy this file to `apps/web/.env` for local development. Vite loads `.env` in
# every mode and also reads `.env.local`, `.env.[mode]`, and `.env.[mode].local`;
# only `VITE_`-prefixed variables reach the browser, and this file needs none of
# those. Hosting platforms should supply the production values.
#
# The browser talks only to this application, at `/api/*`; the value below is read
# by the server alone and never reaches the client bundle.

# Origin of the Express API, which this server forwards `/api/*` to. It is an
# origin, not a base path: the API mounts its routers at the root, so there is no
# prefix here. Locally it is the address `pnpm --filter api dev` listens on.
#
# In production, point it at an address only this server can reach — a private
# service address or an internal hostname — and then keep the API off the public
# internet. The same public web origin belongs in the API's `CORS_ORIGIN`, which
# is what its own state-changing routes check.
#
# Leave it unset only for local development, where the default above is correct.
# A production server answers `502` rather than guessing at an address it was not
# given.
API_UPSTREAM_URL=http://localhost:8000